{"book":11,"chapter":6,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 6","slides":[{"title":"Functions are values","sub":"Chapter 6 · First-Class","short":"Intro","main":"A function can be stored, passed and returned, like any value.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["In a variable","As an argument","In an object field"],"captions":["A function can go into a variable, like a number or a string","It can be passed to another function and returned from one: callbacks and event handlers are built on this","A function is stored in an object field, which is how methods appear"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const double = function (x) {","  return x * 2;","};","double(4)   // 8"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["[1, 2, 3].map(double)","// [2, 4, 6]","","setTimeout(fn, 1000)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const user = {","  name: 'Ada',","  hi() { return 'hello'; },","};","user.hi()"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[17.4,29.0]}]},{"title":"Declaration and expression","sub":"Hoisting and return","short":"Declaration","main":"A declaration is hoisted, an expression is not; do not move return to the next line.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Declaration","Hoisting","return and ;"],"captions":["Declaration: the function keyword, a name, parameters and a body; without return the function gives undefined","A declaration is \"hoisted\": you can call it before it is written; an expression before assignment is an error","return with an expression on the next line fails: the engine inserts ; right after the word return"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["function add(a, b) {","  return a + b;","}","function noop() {}","noop()   // undefined"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["hello();        // works","function hello() {}","","later();        // TypeError","var later = function () {};"],"hl":[0,3],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":50.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["return","  a + b;   // returns nothing","","return a +","  b;       // correct"],"hl":[0,3],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":250.0}]],"cues":[15.2,28.2]}]},{"title":"Arrow functions","sub":"=> and this","short":"Arrows","main":"An arrow is short and takes this from outside; methods use regular functions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Short form","Object literal","No own this"],"captions":["Arrow: parameters, => and an expression; one expression needs no return, a block needs an explicit one","Wrap an object literal in parentheses, or the braces will be taken for the function body","An arrow has no own this: it takes it from the environment; methods and constructors use regular functions"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const sq = (x) => x * x;","const inc = n => n + 1;","const sum = (a, b) => {","  return a + b;","};"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["const mk = (n) => ({ n });","const bad = (n) => { n };","mk(1)    // { n: 1 }","bad(1)   // undefined"],"hl":[0],"bad":[1,3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"function\nown this","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"arrow\nouter this","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":270.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":270.0,"y":118.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"environment","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.4,28.2]}]},{"title":"Parameters","sub":"Defaults, rest, references","short":"Parameters","main":"The argument count is not checked; objects are passed by reference.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Extra and missing","Defaults and rest","Object reference"],"captions":["The argument count is not checked: extras are ignored, missing ones are undefined","A default is used only for undefined; ...rest collects the remaining arguments into an array","Arguments are passed by value, but for objects the value is a reference: a function can change a passed array"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["function f(a, b) { return [a, b]; }","f(1)        // [1, undefined]","f(1, 2, 3)  // [1, 2]"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["function f(a, b = 5, ...rest) {","  return [a, b, rest];","}","f(1)           // [1, 5, []]","f(1, null, 7)  // [1, null, [7]]"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["function push1(list) {","  list.push(1);","}","const a = [];","push1(a);   // a → [1]"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[20.8,29.9]}]},{"title":"Destructuring","sub":"Options object and spread","short":"Destructuring","main":"One options object instead of a long parameter list.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Options object","Spread in a call","Copy with a change"],"captions":["Parameters are taken apart in the header: one object with defaults instead of five positional ones","The ... operator in a call unpacks an array into separate arguments: Math.max(...nums)","{ ...obj, a: 1 } makes a copy with a replaced field, the basis of immutable style"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["function box({ w, h = 10, c = 'red' }) {","  return `${w}x${h} ${c}`;","}","box({ w: 5 })  // '5x10 red'"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const nums = [3, 9, 4];","Math.max(...nums)  // 9","Math.max(3, 9, 4)  // same"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const a = { n: 1, k: 2 };","const b = { ...a, n: 5 };","// a → { n: 1, k: 2 }","// b → { n: 5, k: 2 }"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[10.7,24.7]}]},{"title":"Scope","sub":"Block and dead zone","short":"Visibility","main":"let and const are block-scoped; before the declaration they are unavailable.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Block","Dead zone","Globals"],"captions":["let and const are visible only inside the nearest curly braces; var, in the whole function","Before the declaration line, let and const are in the \"temporal dead zone\": access gives a ReferenceError","Extra globals can collide with the code of another script on the page"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":78.0,"w":300.0,"h":110.0,"text":"","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t1","x":70.0,"y":36.0,"text":"function","tone":"muted","size":9.0},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":84.0,"w":140.0,"h":66.0,"text":"{ block }\nlet x = 1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":120.0,"y":118.0,"text":"x is not\nvisible here","tone":"red","size":9.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["console.log(x);   // ReferenceError","let x = 5;","console.log(x);   // 5"],"hl":[0],"bad":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":290.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"window (global)","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"own script","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"other script","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":110.0,"y1":86.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":250.0,"y1":86.0,"x2":210.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":148.0,"text":"shared name: a collision","tone":"red","size":9.0}]],"cues":[15.5,28.9]}]},{"title":"Lexical environment","sub":"Environment chain","short":"Environment","main":"Names are looked up where the function is written, not where it is called.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Environments","Name lookup","Shadowing"],"captions":["Every call has its own environment: a table of variables with a reference to the outer one","The search goes up the chain: local names, the creation environment, the global one; not found is a ReferenceError","An inner variable with the same name shadows the outer one, a common source of bugs"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"global: a = 1","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":180.0,"y":92.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"outer: b = 2","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":180.0,"y":144.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"inner: c = 3","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":180.0,"y1":130.0,"x2":180.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":180.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":180.0,"y2":54.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":120.0,"y":40.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"global: a = 1","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":120.0,"y":92.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"outer: b = 2","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":120.0,"y":144.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"inner: c = 3","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":130.0,"x2":120.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":120.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":120.0,"y2":54.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":214.0,"y":60.0,"lines":["// inside h:","a + b + c","// → 6"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":140.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const x = 'outer';","function f() {","  const x = 'inner';","  return x;   // 'inner'","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":19.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[15.1,27.1]}]},{"title":"Closure","sub":"Private state","short":"Closure","main":"A closure is a function together with the environment where it was created.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Counter factory","The environment lives","Independent copies"],"captions":["The factory creates a variable and returns a function that increments it","The inner function keeps the environment: n stays available long after the outer call has finished","Each factory call gives its own environment, and its own independent counter"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["function makeCounter() {","  let n = 0;","  return () => ++n;","}","const next = makeCounter();"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":90.0,"y":62.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"next\n(function)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":62.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"environment\nn = 2","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":110.0,"lines":["next();  // 1","next();  // 2"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":16.0,"w":150.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"a()  →  n = 1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":104.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"b()  →  n = 1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":116.0,"y1":104.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":104.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":270.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"environment A","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":270.0,"y":104.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"environment B","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.9,33.2]}]},{"title":"Closures in a loop","sub":"var and let","short":"In a loop","main":"In loops, declare variables with let.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["var","let","IIFE"],"captions":["With var all functions see one variable, and after the loop it holds the last value: 3, 3, 3","let creates a new variable on each iteration: each function remembers its own value, 0, 1, 2","The loop used to be wrapped in an immediately invoked function (IIFE); now let is enough"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {","  fns.push(() => i);","}","fns.map((f) => f())","// [3, 3, 3]"],"hl":[4],"bad":[4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {","  fns.push(() => i);","}","fns.map((f) => f())","// [0, 1, 2]"],"hl":[0,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {","  ((j) => fns.push(() => j))(i);","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"works, but outdated","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}]],"cues":[18.3,25.1]}]},{"title":"Higher-order functions","sub":"map, filter, reduce","short":"map, filter","main":"map, filter and reduce chains describe data, not a loop.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["map","filter","reduce"],"captions":["map applies a callback to each element and returns a new array of the same size","filter keeps only the elements for which the callback returned true","reduce folds an array into one value, starting from an accumulator passed as the second argument"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":150.0,"y":40.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":210.0,"y":40.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":90.0,"y":110.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":150.0,"y":110.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":210.0,"y":110.0,"w":50.0,"h":26.0,"text":"6","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"text":"x => x * 2","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":48.0,"h":26.0,"text":"1","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":126.0,"y":40.0,"w":48.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":182.0,"y":40.0,"w":48.0,"h":26.0,"text":"3","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":238.0,"y":40.0,"w":48.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":70.0,"y":110.0,"w":48.0,"h":26.0,"text":"2","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":126.0,"y":110.0,"w":48.0,"h":26.0,"text":"4","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"text":"x % 2 === 0","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["[1, 2, 3, 4].reduce(","  (acc, x) => acc + x,","  0",")  // 10"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[19.4,32.7]}]},{"title":"this","sub":"call, apply, bind","short":"this","main":"this depends on the call; arrows and explicit arguments are safer.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Method","Lost this","bind and arrow"],"captions":["In a regular function this depends on how it is called: for an object method it is the object itself","Pull a method into a variable or pass it as a callback and this is lost: undefined in strict mode","bind fixes this, call and apply call with a given this, and an arrow takes it from outside"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const u = {","  name: 'Ada',","  hi() { return this.name; },","};","u.hi()   // 'Ada'"],"hl":[4],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const hi = u.hi;","hi()            // TypeError","setTimeout(u.hi, 0)  // too"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const f = u.hi.bind(u);","f()                // 'Ada'","u.hi.call({ name: 'B' })","// 'B'"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[11.1,24.8]}]},{"title":"Recursion and memoization","sub":"Stack and cache","short":"Recursion","main":"Stack depth is finite; memoization keeps results in a closure.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Recursion","Stack overflow","Memoization"],"captions":["Recursion: a function calls itself; a stop condition is required","The call stack is finite: tens of thousands of nested calls give a RangeError, so deep traversal becomes a loop","Memoization keeps results in a closure: a repeated call with the same arguments returns the ready value"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["function fact(n) {","  if (n <= 1) return 1;","  return n * fact(n - 1);","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":130.0,"y":140.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"fact(10000)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":130.0,"y":116.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"fact(9999)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":130.0,"y":92.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"fact(9998)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":130.0,"y":68.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"fact(9997)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":130.0,"y":44.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"fact(9996)","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":76.0,"text":"RangeError:\nMaximum call\nstack size exceeded","tone":"red","size":9.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["function memo(f) {","  const cache = new Map();","  return (x) => {","    if (!cache.has(x)) cache.set(x, f(x));","    return cache.get(x);","  };","}"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[13.6,28.7]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: objects, arrays, Map and Set.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Functions","Scope","Next"],"captions":["Functions are values: passed, returned and stored; arrows are short and take this from outside","let and const are block-scoped, name lookup is lexical; a closure is a function with its environment","Next: objects, arrays, Map and Set: how to store data and update it without breaking the original"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"value","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":230.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"x => x * 2","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":160.0,"y":116.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"this from outside","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"lexical","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":230.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"closure","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":160.0,"y":116.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"let in loops","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const user = {","  tags: ['a', 'b'],","};","const m = new Map();"],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":270.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"chapter 7: objects, arrays, collections","size":9.5}]],"cues":[12.6,30.1]}]}]}